{
  "dom_id": "step-q75737",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14116680/assets/539b08ea12f9af52defd826c0b63c194f36b6de408770c1bc1975bd6ca84724f.png)\n\nThe vector $u$ is an eigenvector of a $2\\times 2$ matrix $B$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $-\\frac{1}{2}.$ Find the vector $Bu.$",
  "worked_solution": "The eigenvector $u=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-\\frac{1}{2}.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Bu & =-\\frac{1}{2}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14116680/assets/c0bffb825fa5610288e3c88555a41c8124cf3538b2f75ebe627543a678ca3fba.png)",
